    <!-- 06 Partnership Ads vs Spark Ads -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="vs-spark">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">06 &mdash; Cross-Platform</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Partnership Ads vs Spark Ads</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Partnership Ads = Meta&rsquo;s creator-powered ad format (Instagram &amp; Facebook)</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Spark Ads = TikTok&rsquo;s creator-powered ad format</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Same concept, different platforms, different mechanics</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Partnership Ads and <a href="/spark-ads" class="text-accent hover:underline">Spark Ads</a> solve the same problem on different platforms: allowing brands to run paid ads using a creator&rsquo;s identity instead of the brand&rsquo;s own account. Both formats produce ads that look like organic creator content rather than polished brand advertising. But the implementation details, authorization workflows, and platform dynamics differ significantly.</p>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-border bg-card mb-6">
          <table class="w-full border-collapse text-[14px]">
            <thead class="bg-bg">
              <tr>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Aspect</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Partnership Ads (Meta)</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Spark Ads (TikTok)</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Platform</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Instagram and Facebook</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">TikTok</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Authorization method</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Paid Partnership tag + ad creation access toggle</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Auth code generated by creator, valid 30&ndash;365 days</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Engagement retention</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Paid engagement shown separately from organic</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">All engagement (paid + organic) accumulates on original post</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Content source</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Creator must publish on their profile first</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Can use existing posts or brand&rsquo;s own account posts</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Targeting</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Meta&rsquo;s full targeting stack (demographics, interests, lookalike, custom audiences)</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">TikTok&rsquo;s targeting (interest, behavior, custom, lookalike)</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Formats supported</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Reels, Stories, Feed (image/video), Carousel</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">In-Feed video only</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">CTA options</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Standard Meta CTA buttons (Shop Now, Learn More, etc.)</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Standard TikTok CTA buttons</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Audience demographics</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Broader age range, strong 25&ndash;54 segment</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Skews younger, strong 18&ndash;34 segment</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink">Best for</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">Brands active on Instagram/Facebook, multi-format campaigns</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">Brands active on TikTok, short-form video-first campaigns</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Key differences in practice</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4"><strong>Authorization workflow.</strong> Spark Ads use a simpler auth code system &mdash; the creator generates a code in TikTok, sends it to the brand, and the brand enters it in TikTok Ads Manager. The code has a set validity period (30, 60, or 365 days). Partnership Ads require a more structured setup through Meta Business Suite, with approved partner status and per-post permission toggles. The Meta workflow is more rigid but provides tighter control over which specific posts can be promoted.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4"><strong>Engagement handling.</strong> This is the biggest practical difference. On TikTok, Spark Ads accumulate all engagement (likes, comments, shares from both organic and paid distribution) on the original post. This means a Spark Ad campaign can permanently boost a post&rsquo;s social proof. Meta Partnership Ads separate paid engagement from organic &mdash; the ad&rsquo;s likes and comments are not added to the original post&rsquo;s counts.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4"><strong>Running both simultaneously.</strong> For brands with a cross-platform strategy, running both Partnership Ads (Meta) and Spark Ads (TikTok) with the same creator content is a common and effective approach. The same creator can produce a Reel for Instagram and a TikTok video with similar messaging, then authorize both as paid ads. OKAD&rsquo;s creator network and production pipeline are built to support this cross-platform workflow.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 07 Best Practices -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="best-practices">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">07 &mdash; Best Practices</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Best practices for Partnership Ads</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Match the creator to the audience, not to the brand</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Brief for authenticity, not for polish</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Test organic performance before committing ad spend</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Creator selection</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">The creator&rsquo;s identity is the ad&rsquo;s primary trust signal. Selecting the right creator is the single most important decision in a Partnership Ads campaign. The ideal creator is someone whose audience overlaps with the brand&rsquo;s target demographic, whose content style feels native to the platform, and whose voice is genuinely relatable to the people the ad will reach. Follower count matters far less than audience quality and content style.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Look for creators who already produce content in your product&rsquo;s category or adjacent categories. A skincare brand benefits more from a creator who regularly posts skincare routines than from a general lifestyle creator with a larger following. The audience&rsquo;s existing trust in the creator&rsquo;s expertise in that category transfers directly to the ad&rsquo;s credibility.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Content briefs</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">The biggest mistake brands make with Partnership Ads is over-scripting the creator. Partnership Ads work because they look and feel like organic creator content. A heavily scripted ad with brand-approved talking points defeats the purpose. The brief should define the key message, any mandatory disclosures, and the desired CTA &mdash; then let the creator produce content in their natural style.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Effective briefs include: the product or service being promoted, the key benefit to highlight (one, not five), any specific claims to avoid, the desired CTA (link in bio, swipe up, shop now), and examples of the creator&rsquo;s own content that the brand likes. The brief should be one page, not ten. More creative freedom for the creator typically means better-performing ads.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Test organic before paying for paid</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">The most efficient Partnership Ads strategy is to let creator content perform organically first, then promote the winners. When a creator publishes a partnership post, it reaches their organic audience. Posts that generate strong engagement organically &mdash; high saves, shares, comments, retention &mdash; are statistically more likely to perform well as paid ads. This organic-first approach turns every creator post into a free creative test.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">This strategy is especially powerful when combined with <a href="/canvas-ugc" class="text-accent hover:underline">Canvas UGC</a> programs, where creators are already producing high-volume content on brand accounts. The organic winners from the canvas become Partnership Ad candidates, creating a natural pipeline from organic testing to paid amplification.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Scaling</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Scale Partnership Ads by adding more creators, not by increasing spend on a single creator&rsquo;s post. Each creator brings a unique identity and audience signal. Running Partnership Ads from 5&ndash;10 different creators simultaneously gives you multiple trust signals to test against different audience segments. The same product message delivered by different creators performs differently with different demographics.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">OKAD&rsquo;s creator network includes hundreds of vetted creators across categories and demographics. When scaling Partnership Ads, we match creators to audience segments, produce content at volume, manage permissions across all partnerships, and run the ad campaigns from a single Ads Manager account.</p>

        <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-xl p-6 my-6 flex gap-4 items-start flex-col sm:flex-row">
          <div class="w-11 h-11 rounded-[10px] bg-[rgba(99,102,241,.06)] border border-[rgba(99,102,241,.12)] flex items-center justify-center text-[20px] shrink-0">&#x1F3AC;</div>
