            <h4 class="font-display text-[16px] font-semibold mb-1"><a href={emailSubject} class="text-ink hover:text-accent transition-colors no-underline">OKAD sources creators and produces Partnership Ad content</a></h4>
            <p class="text-[14px] text-muted m-0 leading-[1.5]">From creator matching and briefing to content production and partnership setup &mdash; we run the full pipeline so your team focuses on strategy and results, not creator coordination.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 08 Measurement & Optimization -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="measurement">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">08 &mdash; Measurement</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Measurement and optimization</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Track creator-level performance, not just campaign-level aggregates</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Key metrics: engagement rate, hook rate, CTR, CVR, ROAS</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Meta brand lift studies measure the trust advantage quantitatively</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Measuring Partnership Ads requires a different lens than standard ad measurement. Because the creator&rsquo;s identity is a key variable, you need to track performance at the creator level &mdash; not just at the campaign or ad set level. Two Partnership Ads with identical targeting but different creators can produce wildly different results. The creator is the creative variable.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Key metrics to track</h3>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-border bg-card mb-6">
          <table class="w-full border-collapse text-[14px]">
            <thead class="bg-bg">
              <tr>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Metric</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">What it measures</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Why it matters for Partnership Ads</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Hook rate</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">% of viewers who watch past 3 seconds</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Measures if the creator&rsquo;s identity and opening grab attention</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Engagement rate</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Likes + comments + shares / impressions</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Partnership Ads should outperform standard ads here by 2&ndash;3x</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">CTR</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Click-through rate to destination</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Indicates strength of the creator&rsquo;s CTA and audience trust</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">CVR</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Conversion rate (purchase, signup, install)</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Measures whether trust translates to action down-funnel</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">CPE</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Cost per engagement</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Should be lower than standard ads due to higher engagement</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink">ROAS</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">Return on ad spend</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">The ultimate efficiency metric &mdash; compare across creators</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Brand lift studies</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Meta offers <strong>brand lift studies</strong> that measure the incremental impact of your Partnership Ads on brand awareness, ad recall, and purchase intent. These studies compare a test group (people who saw the ad) against a control group (similar people who did not) and quantify the lift attributable to the campaign. For Partnership Ads specifically, brand lift studies typically show a higher lift in ad recall and favorability compared to standard brand ads &mdash; a direct measurement of the trust advantage.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Brand lift studies require a minimum spend threshold (typically $30,000+ per study) and are best suited for larger campaigns. For smaller-budget campaigns, focus on engagement rate differentials and CTR comparisons between Partnership Ads and standard ads running the same product message to the same audiences.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Attribution and reporting</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Partnership Ads use Meta&rsquo;s standard attribution windows (1-day click, 7-day click, 1-day view). Both the brand and the creator can see performance data for partnership content: the brand sees full ad-level metrics in Ads Manager, and the creator sees organic and paid reach insights on their post. This dual visibility makes it easy to align on what&rsquo;s working and what needs to change.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">For brands running Partnership Ads alongside <a href="/spark-ads" class="text-accent hover:underline">Spark Ads</a> on TikTok, maintaining a unified cross-platform dashboard is essential. Track creator-level performance across both Meta and TikTok to identify which creators drive results on which platform. Some creators perform better on Instagram; others excel on TikTok. The data tells you where to allocate spend and which creators to scale.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 09 Glossary -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="glossary">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">09 &mdash; Glossary</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Key terms</h2>

        {[
          { term: "Partnership Ads", def: "Meta's ad format that lets brands run paid ads on Instagram and Facebook using a creator's identity. The ad displays the creator's handle and profile photo as the source. Formerly called Branded Content Ads." },
          { term: "Branded Content Ads", def: "The original name for Partnership Ads, used by Meta before the mid-2023 rebrand. The mechanics are identical; only the naming changed." },
          { term: "Paid Partnership tag", def: "The disclosure label that appears on creator posts when they tag a brand as a commercial partner. Required by Meta's branded content policies and by advertising regulations in most jurisdictions." },
          { term: "Ad creation access", def: "A per-post permission toggle that the creator enables to allow the brand to use their post as an ad creative in Meta Ads Manager." },
          { term: "Meta Business Suite", def: "Meta's business management platform (formerly Business Manager) where brands manage Pages, Instagram accounts, ad accounts, and branded content partnerships." },
          { term: "Brand Collabs Manager", def: "Meta's marketplace for connecting brands with creators. Provides search, outreach, and partnership management tools. Integrated into Meta Business Suite." },
          { term: "Professional account", def: "An Instagram account type (Creator or Business) that provides access to branded content tools, insights, and monetization features. Required for Partnership Ads." },
          { term: "Spark Ads", def: "TikTok's equivalent of Partnership Ads. Allows brands to promote existing creator posts as paid ads on TikTok, retaining all engagement on the original post." },
          { term: "Hook rate", def: "The percentage of viewers who watch past the first 3 seconds of a video ad. A key early indicator of creative effectiveness for Reels and Stories Partnership Ads." },
          { term: "Brand lift study", def: "A Meta measurement tool that quantifies the incremental impact of an ad campaign on brand awareness, ad recall, and purchase intent by comparing exposed vs. control groups." },
          { term: "Creative testing", def: "The practice of systematically testing multiple ad creatives — hooks, formats, creators, angles — to identify top performers before scaling spend. See the full guide at /guide." },
          { term: "Canvas UGC", def: "A delivery model where creators post content on brand-owned social accounts and get paid per view. Top organic performers from Canvas UGC programs often graduate to Partnership Ads." },
        ].map((item) => (
          <div class="py-4 border-b border-border">
            <div class="font-display font-semibold text-ink mb-1">{item.term}</div>
            <div class="text-[14px] text-muted">{item.def}</div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 10 FAQ -->
