        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">10 &mdash; FAQ</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Frequently asked questions</h2>

        {[
          { q: "What are Partnership Ads?", a: "Partnership Ads are Meta's creator-powered ad format for Instagram and Facebook. They allow a brand to promote a creator's post as a paid ad while keeping the creator's identity (name, handle, profile photo) as the ad source. The ad appears as creator content with a 'Paid partnership' and 'Sponsored' label." },
          { q: "What happened to Branded Content Ads?", a: "Branded Content Ads were rebranded to Partnership Ads in mid-2023. The underlying mechanics are the same — creator tags brand, brand promotes the post. Meta updated the name as part of a broader refresh of its creator monetization tools." },
          { q: "Do creators need a certain follower count?", a: "No. There is no minimum follower count to use Partnership Ads. The creator needs an Instagram Professional account (Creator or Business type) and must comply with Meta's branded content policies. Follower count is irrelevant to eligibility — what matters is account type and policy compliance." },
          { q: "How are Partnership Ads different from Spark Ads?", a: "Partnership Ads run on Meta (Instagram and Facebook). Spark Ads run on TikTok. Both use the creator's identity as the ad source. Key difference: Spark Ads accumulate all engagement (paid + organic) on the original post, while Meta Partnership Ads separate paid engagement from organic. Authorization workflows also differ — Spark Ads use auth codes, Partnership Ads use Meta Business Suite approvals." },
          { q: "Can I run Partnership Ads and Spark Ads at the same time?", a: "Yes, and this is a common cross-platform strategy. The same creator produces similar content for both Instagram and TikTok, then authorizes both as paid ads. This lets brands reach audiences across both platforms with creator-powered content. OKAD manages cross-platform campaigns with unified reporting." },
          { q: "What formats work with Partnership Ads?", a: "Reels, Stories, Feed posts (image and video), and Carousels on both Instagram and Facebook. The format of the original creator post determines the available ad placements. Reels are the highest-performing format for most brands in 2026." },
          { q: "How much do Partnership Ads cost?", a: "Partnership Ads use the same auction system as standard Meta ads. CPMs vary by targeting, placement, and competition. The ad delivery cost is comparable to standard ads, but Partnership Ads typically deliver higher engagement and CTR — meaning the effective cost per engagement or cost per action is lower. Budget for creator compensation separately from ad spend." },
          { q: "Can the creator control which posts get promoted?", a: "Yes. The creator must explicitly enable 'Allow brand partner to promote' on each individual post. The brand cannot promote a creator's post without this permission. The creator can also revoke access at any time." },
          { q: "How do I find creators for Partnership Ads?", a: "Options include Meta's Brand Collabs Manager (built into Business Suite), creator marketplaces, agency networks, and direct outreach. The most important criteria are audience overlap with your target demographic and content style that matches the platform's native feel. Follower count is a secondary consideration." },
          { q: "Can OKAD manage my Partnership Ads?", a: "Yes. OKAD handles the full Partnership Ads workflow: creator sourcing from our network, partnership setup and permissions, content briefing and production, ad campaign management in Meta Ads Manager, and cross-platform coordination with Spark Ads on TikTok. Write to us at olga@okad.agency to discuss your brand and goals." },
        ].map((item) => (
          <div class="faq-item border-b border-border">
            <div class="faq-q flex justify-between items-center gap-4 py-5 cursor-pointer">
              <span class="font-display font-semibold text-[16px] text-ink">{item.q}</span>
              <span class="font-mono text-[20px] text-accent shrink-0 faq-icon">+</span>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-a overflow-hidden max-h-0 transition-all duration-300">
              <div class="pb-5 text-[15px] text-ink-2 leading-[1.65]">{item.a}</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
